3.3 Brooding Management
Brooding was carried out during the first four weeks to provide the chicks with adequate warmth, feed, water, and protection.
Brooding Practices
•	Temperature maintained between 32°C and 35°C during the first week.
•	Temperature reduced gradually each week.
•	Clean water supplied at all times.
•	Chick mash provided ad libitum.
•	Wet litter removed daily.
•	Curtains adjusted depending on weather.
•	Birds observed several times each day.
Signs of Good Brooding
•	Uniform distribution of chicks.
•	Active feeding.
•	Continuous water intake.
•	Normal growth.
